WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.320
This final module brings the course back to the main idea:

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.300
application security is part of a practical defensive security program.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.840
The OWASP Top 10 gives teams a clear language for common application risks,

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.780
while the CIS Controls help translate those risks into safeguards, ownership,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.440
and repeatable work.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.740
A weakness in an application rarely stays inside the application team.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:28.480
It can affect identity, data protection, secure configuration, vulnerability management,

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:33.340
logging, monitoring, incident response, and customer trust.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:38.120
That is why secure development needs to connect with operations and security processes.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.900
Use the mappings in this course as a planning aid.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.480
For each application risk, ask which CIS Controls safeguards help prevent the issue,

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:51.500
which safeguards help detect abuse, and which safeguards support response and recovery.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.720
Then confirm who owns the work and what evidence shows that it is happening.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.500
Good evidence does not need to be theatrical.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:04.160
Tickets, scan results, code review records, change approvals, architecture notes,

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.860
test results, access reviews,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.440
and monitoring records can all help show that security work is repeatable and improving.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:17.540
After this course, a practical next step is to review a real application or service.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.640
Pick one OWASP risk, identify the relevant CIS Controls safeguards,

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.580
confirm current controls and gaps, assign owners, and document the next improvement.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:28.680
Small,

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:33.860
consistent improvements are how application security becomes durable defensive practice.
